      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 3.33,
          "en": "So, let's dive right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.33,
          "end": 6.54,
          "en": "into this video and this topic by answering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.54,
          "end": 8.96,
          "en": "the most important question first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.96,
          "end": 13.96,
          "en": "What exactly is React.js and why would we use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.96,
          "end": 15.51,
          "en": "Why do we need it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 18.52,
          "en": "What's the problem it helps us solve?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.52,
          "end": 23.06,
          "en": "Regarding the what, we can, of course, visit reactjs.org,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.06,
          "end": 26.31,
          "en": "the official webpage of React.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.31,
          "end": 30.47,
          "en": "And there, we learn that React is a JavaScript library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.47,
          "end": 35.47,
          "en": "and it's a JavaScript library for building user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.62,
          "end": 37.13,
          "en": "Now, that's quite straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.13,
          "end": 40.54,
          "en": "It's a library for the JavaScript programming language",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.54,
          "end": 43.97,
          "en": "that helps us build user interfaces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.97,
          "end": 46.513,
          "en": "But what exactly does this nice sentence mean?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.35,
          "end": 50.41,
          "en": "React.js is a library and, to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.41,
          "end": 52.55,
          "en": "it's a client-side library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.55,
          "end": 55.22,
          "en": "It's about client-side JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.22,
          "end": 57.61,
          "en": "So, the JavaScript code, which runs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.61,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "in the browsers of your visitors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 64.36,
          "en": "And that is important because we use JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.36,
          "end": 68.81,
          "en": "in the browser to manipulate web pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.81,
          "end": 71.6,
          "en": "after they were loaded, and that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.6,
          "end": 74.63,
          "en": "to build rich, highly interactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.63,
          "end": 78.31,
          "en": "modern user interfaces for our websites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.31,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "Take something like Netflix, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 84.5,
          "en": "which is actually built with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.5,
          "end": 88.14,
          "en": "There, we can browse around, we can hover over one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.14,
          "end": 93.02000000000001,
          "en": "of the movies or series, and we get more details there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.02000000000001,
          "end": 96.46000000000001,
          "en": "We can add it to our list, and we can go to that list page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.46000000000001,
          "end": 100.16,
          "en": "and everything here happens very smoothly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.16,
          "end": 102.41,
          "en": "and also quickly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.41,
          "end": 107.41,
          "en": "We never need to click anywhere, and load a new HTML page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.34,
          "end": 113.17,
          "en": "That refresh icon, in the top left corner, never spins",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.17,
          "end": 116.91,
          "en": "Because we never request a new HTML page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.91,
          "end": 120.84,
          "en": "we never have to wait for a new HTML page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 123.54,
          "en": "to be generated by the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.54,
          "end": 127.81,
          "en": "And that happens because JavaScript is doing some work here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.81,
          "end": 130.54,
          "en": "and it's updating what we see on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.54,
          "end": 134.78,
          "en": "the dom, whilst we are working on that page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.78,
          "end": 138.01,
          "en": "And that gives us that nice user experience,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.01,
          "end": 143.01,
          "en": "that nice UI, which we know from mobile apps, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.16,
          "end": 145.6,
          "en": "When we work with a mobile app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.6,
          "end": 149.32,
          "en": "we're used to things being very reactive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.32,
          "end": 151.93,
          "en": "There, we can work with the app and switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.93,
          "end": 156.15,
          "en": "between different screens without having that latency,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 156.15,
          "end": 158.27,
          "en": "which we know from some websites,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.27,
          "end": 162.73,
          "en": "without requesting new HTML pages behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.73,
          "end": 166.91,
          "en": "So, mobile apps therefore feel very reactive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 166.91,
          "end": 169.73,
          "en": "things happen instantly, we don't need to wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 169.73,
          "end": 173.99,
          "en": "for new pages to load, or for actions to start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.99,
          "end": 177.96,
          "en": "And, traditionally, in web apps that was different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.96,
          "end": 180.35,
          "en": "There, we often had to click a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.35,
          "end": 184.75,
          "en": "and then wait for a new page to be loaded and to show up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.75,
          "end": 188.07,
          "en": "And whilst that, of course, also does work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.07,
          "end": 192.15,
          "en": "it is not the same user experience our users know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 192.15,
          "end": 195.03,
          "en": "from their mobile apps, and it's often not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 198.11,
          "en": "the user experience we want to deliver therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.11,
          "end": 201.63,
          "en": "Now, that's a problem we can solve with JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.63,
          "end": 204.87,
          "en": "JavaScript in the browser, because that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.87,
          "end": 208.49,
          "en": "to manipulate the dom and therefore what the user sees",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 208.49,
          "end": 212.69,
          "en": "without requesting a new HTML page and waiting for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 212.69,
          "end": 216.63,
          "en": "And therefore, just JavaScript would be enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 216.63,
          "end": 218.72,
          "en": "But let me give you an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.72,
          "end": 221.84,
          "en": "of just JavaScript and why we might want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 221.84,
          "end": 225.873,
          "en": "to use something like React instead of just JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
